  "adopted_mitigation": {
    "what": "bucket cap at 100, applied at index time",
    "why": "M1 (a document-frequency stop-list) attacks the cause and removes more work, but it changes the representation, which moves every Jaccard in the system: tau has to be re-derived and the labelled separation changes with it. M2 changes only which buckets are allowed to expand, so its price is a pure recall number and nothing else in the design has to move. Genuine duplicates collide in many bands at once (a pair at J=0.9 is expected to match 45 of the 76 bands), so refusing the few pathological buckets costs almost none of them.",
    "detail": {
      "cap": 100,
      "emissions": 1730345,
      "emissions_reduction": 0.6834,
      "largest_bucket": 100,
